From d7357a94699f571146e489fed347c2a89b98ecde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 19:48:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0327 -- BG-tilemap tile census +
 occlusion headroom probe

Diagnostic-only instrument (default OFF) that decomposes the BG tile
pass -- the ~9 ms "mdt_bg_tilelayer" bucket the Mach64/POD-83 frame
decomposition flagged as the largest sub-bucket of mds_tilemap_bg
(bigger than the backdrop-thrash route). MDS_BG_INSTR (patch 0125)
already TIMES that bucket but does not decompose it by tile;
MDS_TFG_INSTR (patch 0111) has the per-tile census but only for the FG
pass. This adds the BG sibling so we can answer, before designing any
skip mechanism, whether occlusion headroom exists at all.

Why it is diag-only and not a perf lever: the question it settles is
whether the 9 ms is count-bound and whether any BG tiles are skippable.
The two occluder counters are the only ones that can exist for the BG
layer -- one tile per cell routed to one pass by (tileattr[t] &
TA_FOREGROUND) == foreground, so FG tiles never occlude BG tiles. That
leaves (1) empty-tile-0 blits over a backdrop and (2) player-sprite
overdraw as the only real occluders. player_occluded is a conservative
UPPER bound (bbox superset of opaque pixels) and player-only by design;
full per-object occlusion is deliberately not measured (O(tiles x
objects), and found headroom would not be cheaply exploitable -- a
runtime skip needs a per-frame coverage map whose maintenance cost
risks the same cost-eats-the-win trap that disabled patch 0127).

Mechanism. Extends the shared _tilemap_inner_render_dispatch template so
its existing wave-25 category/timing counters route to a parallel
g_mds_tbg_* set when instrumenting the BG pass (foreground == 0);
reference bindings are touched only inside the existing if(instr_on)
guards, so the FG pass stays bit-identical and production (instr_on
false) is unaffected. Two new subset counters (drawn_tile0,
player_occluded) bump at the drawTile site. The BG census does NOT set
g_mds_tfg_loop_active, so BG blit time is never conflated into the tfg
_blit_indexed accumulator; it reads per-tile time from the template's
own drawtile bracket instead. Player on-screen rect uses the same
formula as the DrawScene object loop (world-pixel minus scroll minus
sprite drawpoint), computed once per BG-pass call.

Gate: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_MDS_TBG_INSTR=1 (strict-1; default OFF). Emits
[mds-tbg-stat] + [mds-tbg-tiles] per 100-tick block, with a self-check
mirroring the tfg block. Always-on initVideo banner ("BG-tile census
instrumentation ENABLED/DISABLED") for the smoke two-witness gate.
docs/BOOT.md, CLRENV.BAT and the smoke BANNERS entry ride in the outer
repo. Distinct [mds-tbg] prefix vs patch 0125's [mds-bg] timing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
